meta {
  name: Delete Note
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/notes/{{noteId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Soft-deletes a note (`NoteResource.deleteNote`, service `NoteService.deleteNote`). Truck notes: only
  the author, and only within 15 minutes of the note being added; no admin override. (Entity types
  without that rule also allow a TORG_ADMIN of the note's torg, or VAHN_ADMIN.)

  Replies are not deleted. The deleted note keeps its place in lists and threads as a placeholder:
  `deleted: true`, `content` "This remark was deleted", and `author`, `category` and `attachments` null.

  The note's attachment rows stay as a record, but the files are removed from storage right after the
  delete commits (BUG-691): a signed link handed out earlier stops opening (S3 answers 403/404 instead
  of 200). A file that another live note still uses is kept. If storage fails the delete still succeeds
  and the failure is only logged. See the "vehicle-remarks-attachment-delete" flow.

  Deleting is final: afterwards "Update Note" and a second delete both get 404 "Note not found" (BUG-717
  covers the delete/edit race: the loser gets that 404).

  HTTP 200 with body `statusCode` 204 on success. 403 "Only the author can delete a note", or "A note can only be deleted within 15 minutes of being added". 404 "Note not found" for an
  unknown, other-torg or already deleted note.
}
